### Feature Request / Improvement

`TrinoArray.getResultSet()` is [not supported](https://github.com/trinodb/trino/blob/1790bac56b6811a40cf3c6992c3b9601d77b21fe/client/trino-jdbc/src/main/java/io/trino/jdbc/TrinoArray.java#L85-L111), all 4 implementations throw `SQLFeatureNotSupportedException("getResultSet not supported")`. 

This is supported on other JDBC drivers like Postgres and ClickHouse. This is useful for getting the element of an array and iterating over them. 

`TrinoArray.getResultSet()` should return a ResultSet with one row for each element.

Trino:
```java
String connStr = "jdbc:trino://localhost:8088";
try (Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(connStr, "user", "password");
    Statement stmt = con.createStatement();
    ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT ARRAY['a', 'b', 'c']")) {
    rs.next();
    Array array = rs.getArray(1);
    ResultSet elements = array.getResultSet(); // throws here
    while (elements.next()) {
        System.out.println(elements.getLong(1) + " -> " + elements.getString(2));
    }
}
```

`java --class-path trino-jdbc-484.jar Main.java`

```
Exception in thread "main" java.sql.SQLFeatureNotSupportedException: getResultSet not supported
        at io.trino.jdbc.TrinoArray.getResultSet(TrinoArray.java:89)
        at Main.main(Main.java:16)
```

Postgres:
```java
String connStr = "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/postgres";
try (Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(connStr, "user", "password");
    Statement stmt = con.createStatement();
    ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT ARRAY['a', 'b', 'c']")) {
    rs.next();
    Array array = rs.getArray(1);
    ResultSet elements = array.getResultSet();
    while (elements.next()) {
        System.out.println(elements.getLong(1) + " -> " + elements.getString(2));
    }
}
```

`java --class-path postgresql-42.7.12.jar Main.java `

```
1 -> a
2 -> b
3 -> c
```

