[Transparency: I had my agent open this issue on my behalf.]

### Preliminary checks

- [x] Reproduced outside an IDE in a fresh Node process.
- [x] Confirmed the faulty implementation is present on current main (8.71.1).
- [x] Searched existing issues; no matching open report found.
- [ ] Human review of this AI-assisted report under the AI Contribution Policy is pending.

### Relevant Package

`type-utils`

### Repro Code

Run this as an ES module with `typescript` and `@typescript-eslint/type-utils` installed:

```js
import ts from 'typescript';
import { getTypeOfPropertyOfType } from '@typescript-eslint/type-utils';

const fileName = '/repro.ts';
const options = { strict: true, target: ts.ScriptTarget.ESNext };
const host = ts.createCompilerHost(options);
const originalGetSourceFile = host.getSourceFile;
host.getSourceFile = (name, ...args) => name === fileName
  ? ts.createSourceFile(
      name,
      'declare const key: unique symbol; interface Test { readonly [key]: string }',
      options.target,
      true,
    )
  : originalGetSourceFile(name, ...args);

const program = ts.createProgram([fileName], options, host);
const checker = program.getTypeChecker();
const declaration = program.getSourceFile(fileName).statements[1];
const type = checker.getTypeAtLocation(declaration);
const property = type.getProperties()[0];

console.log(checker.typeToString(getTypeOfPropertyOfType(checker, type, property)));
console.log(checker.typeToString(checker.getTypeOfSymbol(property)));
```

### Expected Result

Both lines print `string`.

### Actual Result

The helper prints `any` (the intrinsic error type); the direct compiler lookup prints `string`.

### Additional Info

The escaped-property branch calls `getDeclaredTypeOfSymbol` rather than `getTypeOfSymbol`. This also affects inherited generic properties, mapped symbol properties, private fields, and `Symbol.unscopables` inherited from `ReadonlyArray`.

A downstream immutability rule crashes when it passes the returned error type to `is-immutable-type`. Within type-utils, `isTypeReadonly` can incorrectly accept mutable values behind readonly symbol keys because it sees the error type instead of the nested object.

Historical context: typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint#2143 and typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint#2567.

A fix and isolated regression tests are available on [this branch](https://github.com/Zamiell/typescript-eslint/tree/fix/type-utils-symbol-property-types). The property lookup tests reproduce 15 failures before the fix. A draft PR will be linked, pending issue acceptance and human review.

### Versions

| Package | Version |
| --- | --- |
| `@typescript-eslint/type-utils` | 8.71.0 reproduction; faulty source also confirmed on main at 8.71.1 |
| TypeScript | 6.0.3 reproduction; regression suite also passes with 6.0.2 |
| Node | 24.19.0 |

