## Bug: `one()` with multiple event types removes all listeners on first trigger

**Severity:** Medium  
**Files:** `src/js/mixins/evented.js`  
**Lines:** 320-334

### Description
When `one()` is called with multiple event types (e.g., `['play', 'pause']`) targeting another evented object, a single wrapper function is created for all event types. When any one of the events fires, the wrapper removes itself for ALL event types, not just the one that fired.

This means if you do `player.one(target, ['play', 'pause'], callback)`, and `play` fires first, the listener for `pause` is also removed and will never fire.

The bug is already acknowledged in the code's TODO comment referencing issue #5962.

### Affected code
```javascript
// Line 320-334
} else {
  // TODO: This wrapper is incorrect! It should only
  //       remove the wrapper for the event type that called it.
  //       Instead all listeners are removed on the first trigger!
  //       see https://github.com/videojs/video.js/issues/5962
  const wrapper = (...largs) => {
    this.off(target, type, wrapper);  // <-- Removes wrapper for ALL types
    listener.apply(null, largs);
  };
```

### Suggested fix
Create a separate wrapper for each event type, or modify the wrapper to only remove itself for the specific event type that fired.

