body_text:
### Clear and concise description of the problem

When `@vitest-environment-options` is specified in a test file, those options are passed to the custom environment's `setup` method. 

With access to the `environmentOptions` defined in the config, custom environments would be able to override specific options on a per-test basis, which would make `@vitest-environment-options` more flexible.

Thank you for the guidance in the pull request🙏

### motivating example of proposal

For example, when creating a custom environment as shown below, the options passed to setup are only those specified via `@vitest-environment-options`. If we could also access the options defined in the config, the custom environment could merge them with the config options. This would allow test files to override or specify only a subset of the options. 

custom environment
```ts
import type { Environment } from 'vitest/runtime'
import { builtinEnvironments } from 'vitest/runtime'

export default <Environment>{
  name: 'custom',
  viteEnvironment: 'client',
  async setup(global, options) {
    console.log(JSON.stringify(options, null, 2))

    const dom: 'happy-dom' | 'jsdom' = options.custom.dom || 'happy-dom'
    const { setup } = builtinEnvironments[dom]

    return setup(global, options)
  },
}
```

vitest.config.ts
```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config'

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    name: 'custom',
    environment: 'custom',
    environmentOptions: {
      custom: {
        dom: 'happy-dom',
        other: 'other option',
      },
      happyDOM: {
        url: 'http://localhost:8080',
        settings: {
          navigator: {
            userAgent: 'custom ua',
          },
        },
      },
      jsdom: {
        url: 'http://localhost:8080',
        userAgent: 'custom ua',
      },
    },
  },
})
```
test file
```ts
// @vitest-environment-options { "dom": "jsdom" }
import { it, expect, describe } from 'vitest'

describe('test2', () => {
  it('origin', () => {
    expect(location.origin).toBe('http://localhost:8080')
  })

  it('userAgent', () => {
    expect(navigator.userAgent).toBe('custom ua')
  })
})
```

https://github.com/yamachi4416/reproductions/tree/main/vitest/issues-11277
https://github.com/yamachi4416/reproductions/actions/runs/35551956011/job/106188204328

### Suggested solution

Is there a better way to achieve this?
I would be grateful if you could share any existing way to reference the options set in the config.🙏
Personally, I feel that passing the config options to `setup` and `setupVM` would be ideal since it avoids breaking existing implementations.

