body_text:
### Describe the bug

`browser.providerOptions` was removed in Vitest 4, but setting it is silently ignored — no error, no warning. A config carried over from v3 quietly loses every option inside it.

### Reproduction

vitest.config.ts:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';
import { playwright } from '@vitest/browser-playwright';

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    browser: {
      enabled: true,
      provider: playwright(),
      headless: true,
      instances: [{ browser: 'chromium' }],
      providerOptions: { launchOptions: { executablePath: '/nonexistent/browser' } },
    },
    include: ['sentinel.test.ts'],
  },
});
```

sentinel.test.ts:

```ts
import { expect, test } from 'vitest';
test('sentinel', () => { expect(1 + 1).toBe(2); });
```

```console
$ vitest run
Test Files  1 passed (1)   # real browser launched despite the nonexistent executablePath
```

Reproduced on 5.0.2 and on main (5.0.3). The CLI dotted form (`--browser.providerOptions.*`) is silently ignored the same way.

### Expected behavior

Setting a removed option should fail fast, pointing at the provider factory — the documented home for these options: https://vitest.dev/config/browser/playwright

Fix: #11471

### Environment

Vitest 5.0.2, @vitest/browser-playwright 5.0.2, macOS arm64

AI assistance disclosure: prepared with AI assistance (GLM via ZCode); reproduction run and verified by the account owner.

