### Describe the bug

Failing assertions involving a class getter that accesses a private field can report a `TypeError` instead of the assertion mismatch. This happens with e.g. `toMatchObject` and `toEqual`.

Here is an example test that is supposed to fail because the `value` property is `2` instead of the expected `0`:

```ts
import { test, expect } from "vitest";

class Example {
  #cached: number | undefined;

  get value() {
    if (this.#cached == undefined) {
      this.#cached = 1 + 1; // cache a complicated calculation
    }
    return this.#cached;
  }
}

test("should fail", () => {
  expect(new Example()).toMatchObject({
    value: 0,
  });
});
```

Instead of the expected assertion failure with a diff, the following `TypeError` is thrown:

```
 FAIL  test/example.test.ts > should fail
TypeError: Cannot read private member #cached from an object whose class did not declare it
 ❯ Example.get value [as value] test/example.test.ts:7:14
      5|
      6|   get value() {
      7|     if (this.#cached == undefined) {
       |              ^
      8|       this.#cached = 1 + 1;
      9|     }
```

### Reproduction

 1. Clone the repository https://github.com/jviide/vitest-repro-01.
 2. Install the dependencies with `pnpm install`.
 3. Run the included example test with `pnpm test`.
 4. The test fails, as intended, but it doesn't report the mismatch of the object property `value`. Instead the following error is thrown: `TypeError: Cannot read private member #cached from an object whose class did not declare it`.


