body_text:
### Describe the bug

When `skip(true, note)` is called inside `aroundEach`, the test is skipped, but the note doesn't show up.
The same call in `beforeEach` keeps it.

We use this to skip the rest of a file after a test times out, and it has to happen in `aroundEach` so later
fixtures don't run first.

It looks like `callAroundHooks` [throws the hook errors as an array](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/fb150158b3499ae9e2bd52defd90b0a09b860424/packages/vitest/src/runtime/runner/run.ts#L434-L438),
and `failTask` [only takes the note from a top-level `PendingError`](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/fb150158b3499ae9e2bd52defd90b0a09b860424/packages/vitest/src/runtime/runner/run.ts#L790-L796).
The array was introduced in #9673. This change fixes it locally:

```diff
 function failTask(result: TaskResult, err: unknown, diffOptions: DiffOptions | undefined) {
-  if (err instanceof PendingError) {
+  const pendingError = Array.isArray(err) ? err.find(e => e instanceof PendingError) : err
+  if (pendingError instanceof PendingError) {
     result.state = 'skip'
-    result.note = err.note
+    result.note = pendingError.note
     result.pending = true
     return
   }
```

### Reproduction

https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitest-dev-vitest-mysmxu1g?file=test%2Fbasic.test.ts

```ts
import { aroundEach, beforeEach, describe, test } from 'vitest';

describe('aroundEach', () => {
  aroundEach(async (runTest, { skip }) => {
    skip(true, 'reason from aroundEach');
    await runTest();
  });
  test('skipped in aroundEach', () => {});
});

describe('beforeEach', () => {
  beforeEach(({ skip }) => {
    skip(true, 'reason from beforeEach');
  });
  test('skipped in beforeEach', () => {});
});
```

```
   ✓ aroundEach (1)
     ↓ skipped in aroundEach 1ms
   ✓ beforeEach (1)
     ↓ skipped in beforeEach 0ms [reason from beforeEach]
```

