### WezTerm version

wezterm 20260909-081506-9fa147c9

### Did you try the latest nightly build to see if the issue is better (or worse!) than your current version?

Yes, and I updated the version box above to show the version of the nightly that I tried

### Describe the bug

When calling `mux_window:spawn_tab` or `pane:split` from the Lua API with both `args` and `cwd` set, the `cwd` is silently ignored. The new pane always opens in the current pane's working directory instead.

### To Reproduce

start wezterm press ctrl-shift-p



### Configuration

  wezterm.on('gui-startup', function(cmd)
    mux.spawn_window {
      cwd = 'C:\\Users\\SomeUser\\anyfolder',
      args = { 'cmd.exe' },
    }
  end)

  config.keys = {
    { key = 'p', mods = 'CTRL|SHIFT',
      action = wezterm.action_callback(function(window, pane)
        local tab, new_pane = window:mux_window():spawn_tab {
          cwd = 'C:\\Users\\SomeUser\\somefolder\\',
          args = { 'cmd.exe' },
        }
        wezterm.log_info('requested: C:\\Users\\SomeUser\\somefolder\\')
        wezterm.log_info('actual:    ' .. tostring(new_pane:get_current_working_dir()))
      end)
    },
  }

### Expected Behavior

new tab opens in somefolder

it doesnt. it opens in anyfolder

### Logs

Instead of logs I can explain where it happens.

CommandBuilderFrag::to_command_builder() in lua-api-crates/mux/src/lib.rs
  has two branches:

  - No args: returns (None, self.cwd.clone()) — cwd travels as
  command_dir, works correctly.
  - With args: returns (Some(builder), None) — cwd is set on the builder
  but command_dir is None.

  When command_dir is None, Mux::resolve_cwd() in mux/src/lib.rs:1170
  falls through and returns the current pane's cwd instead. That resolved
  value is then passed as command_dir to LocalDomain::build_command(), which
  calls cmd.cwd(command_dir) unconditionally at line 477 — overwriting the
  explicit cwd that was set on the builder.

  The GUI spawn path (wezterm-gui/src/spawn.rs:60-114) does not have this bug
  because it extracts cwd into a separate variable and passes it directly as
  command_dir, independent of the builder.

There is two possible fixes at least, but it depends on the intention of the developers.

Fix 1

lua-api-crates/mux/src/lib.rs

       if let Some(args) = &self.args {
           let mut builder = CommandBuilder::from_argv(args.iter().map(Into::into).collect());
           for (k, v) in self.set_environment_variables.iter() {
               builder.env(k, v);
           }
           if let Some(cwd) = self.cwd.clone() {
               builder.cwd(cwd);
           }
  -        (Some(builder), None)
  +        (Some(builder), self.cwd.clone())
       } else {
           (None, self.cwd.clone())
       }

it will pass on the requested cwd both to builder and as a override.

Fix 2

mux/src/domain.rs

  -if let Some(dir) = command_dir {
  -    cmd.cwd(dir);
  -}
  +if let Some(dir) = command_dir {
  +    if cmd.get_cwd().is_none() {
  +        cmd.cwd(dir);
  +    }
  +}

this one will respect the cmds own cwd if it has one. I am not sure if the command_dir is supposed to be dominant or not here.
I havent dived very deep into this, but juggling two cwds like this looks error prone.

Fix 1 is tested and working for me.

### Anything else?

_No response_

